  Agent guidance:
  Cover the three paths in the issue: (1) logging backend selection: assert LogFactory.getLog(SomeClass.class) returns a com.alibaba.druid.support.logging.SLF4JImpl. LogFactory reads the 'druid.logType' system property (for example 'slf4j' or 'jdk') before probing. Its choice is made once in static state, so if you set the property, set it before any Druid class initializes, or just rely on the default probe with Logback on the classpath. (2) Filter aliases: create a DruidDataSource with url 'jdbc:h2:mem:druid;DB_CLOSE_DELAY=-1', call setFilters("stat") (alias resolved through META-INF/druid-filter.properties via FilterManager), init it, and run several statements. Assert getProxyFilters() contains a StatFilter and getDataSourceStat().getSqlStatMap() is not empty. Other aliases such as 'mergeStat', 'wall', 'encoding' and 'slf4j' go through the same lookup and are cheap to add. (3) JMX: after init, query ManagementFactory.getPlatformMBeanServer() for the com.alibaba.druid:type=DruidDataSourceStat MBean and assert MBeanInfo.getAttributes().length > 0. Do the same for DruidDataSource, DruidDriver and MockDriver. Druid's bundled MockDriver (jdbc:mock:...) and DruidDriver (jdbc:wrap-jdbc:...) are registered through META-INF/services/java.sql.Driver and can be used for extra no-database coverage. Always close() each DruidDataSource, because DruidDataSourceStatManager keeps static registrations that leak between tests. Use only public Druid APIs; do not call Class.forName or reflection on Druid internals from test code.
  
